---
// Privacy Policy. Describes VisaNav's real data handling: client-side PII
// scrubbing (frontend/src/lib/pii.ts) that strips identifiers but NOT names,
// anonymous chat with no stored IP, encryption at rest, retention limits, and
// deletion. Keep this in step with the app; do not over-claim.
// NOTE: This is a starting template, not legal advice. Have it reviewed by a
// lawyer before relying on it.
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Eyebrow from "../components/Eyebrow.astro";

const updated = "September 22, 2026";

const h2 = "mt-10 text-2xl font-bold text-foreground";
const p = "mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground";
const ul = "mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground";
const a = "text-link underline underline-offset-2 hover:opacity-80";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy — VisaNav"
  description="How VisaNav handles your data: personal details are removed on your device before a message is sent, anonymous chat stores no IP address, conversations are encrypted and deleted on a schedule, and we never sell your data."
  canonicalPath="/privacy"
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-14 sm:px-6">
    <Eyebrow items={["PRIVACY POLICY", "ENCRYPTED, NEVER SOLD"]} />

    <h1 class="mt-5 text-4xl font-bold text-foreground">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <p class={p}>
      VisaNav is a free tool for a community that has real reasons to worry about
      privacy, so we collect as little as we can and protect what we hold. This
      policy explains what we collect, how we use it, who we share it with, and
      the choices you have. VisaNav is operated by Victor Valdez ("VisaNav",
      "we", "us").
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>The short version</h2>
    <ul class={ul}>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-foreground">We remove personal details before your
        message leaves your device.</strong> VisaNav strips identifiers like
        A-numbers, receipt and case numbers, Social Security numbers, emails,
        phone numbers, addresses, and dates in your browser, so they never reach
        our servers or the AI. You see exactly what was removed. (Note: this
        removes those identifiers, but not names you type.)
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-foreground">You can use it anonymously.</strong> No
        account is required, and we do not store your IP address for chat.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-foreground">Conversations are encrypted and
        deleted on a schedule.</strong> We never sell your data and show no
        third-party advertising.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class={h2}>Information we collect</h2>
    <ul class={ul}>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-foreground">Your messages.</strong> The questions
        you send to the assistant, after personal identifiers are removed in your
        browser as described above. We do not ask you to include identifying
        details, and you should not.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-foreground">Account information (optional).</strong>
        If you create an account, we store your email address and a securely
        hashed password, and we send a verification email.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-foreground">Conversation history.</strong> If you
        are signed in (or continue a conversation), we store the messages so you
        can return to them. They are encrypted at rest and deleted on the
        schedule below.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-foreground">Basic technical data.</strong> To run
        the site we use privacy-focused, cookieless
        <a class={a} href="https://www.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/" rel="noopener">Cloudflare Web Analytics</a>,
        which does not use tracking cookies or fingerprint you, and Cloudflare
        Turnstile (a privacy-friendly bot check) on our organization sign-up
        form. Our fonts are self-hosted, so loading a page does not leak data to
        a font provider.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-foreground">Local storage on your device.</strong>
        The app keeps a few things in your browser, not on our servers: your
        login tokens (if signed in), and preferences like language and theme. A
        single cookie remembers whether the sidebar is open; it is not used for
        tracking.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class={h2}>How we use your information</h2>
    <ul class={ul}>
      <li>To answer your questions and provide the assistant.</li>
      <li>To keep your account and conversation history if you choose to have one.</li>
      <li>To protect the Service (security, abuse prevention, and rate limits).</li>
      <li>To understand overall, aggregate usage so we can improve the tool.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class={p}>
      We do not sell your personal information, and we do not use it for
      third-party advertising.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>Who we share it with</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      We share data only with the service providers that make VisaNav work, and
      only as needed to run it:
    </p>
    <ul class={ul}>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-foreground">Our AI provider</strong> (Anthropic or
        OpenAI, depending on configuration) processes your scrubbed message to
        generate an answer.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-foreground">Voyage AI</strong> converts text into
        the numeric representations used to search our knowledge base.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-foreground">Our hosting providers</strong> (Railway
        and Cloudflare) run the servers and deliver the site.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-foreground">Our email provider</strong> sends
        account and verification emails.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class={p}>
      We may also disclose information if required by law, or to protect the
      safety, rights, or security of people and the Service.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>How long we keep it, and deletion</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      Conversation content is encrypted at rest and kept only as long as needed:
    </p>
    <ul class={ul}>
      <li>Anonymous conversations are deleted after about 7 days.</li>
      <li>Signed-in conversations are deleted after about 30 days, unless you opt to keep your history.</li>
      <li>
        You can delete your account and its data at any time. To request
        deletion or a copy of your data, email
        <a class={a} href="mailto:privacy@visanav.org">privacy@visanav.org</a>.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class={h2}>Security</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      We protect data in transit with encryption (HTTPS) and encrypt stored
      conversation content at rest. No system is perfectly secure, but we design
      the Service to hold as little sensitive data as possible in the first
      place.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>Children</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      The Service is not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly
      collect personal information from them. If you believe a child under 13 has
      provided us personal information, contact us and we will delete it. The
      general information on VisaNav can, of course, help families and young
      people learn about immigration.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>Your choices and rights</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      You can use the assistant anonymously, decline to create an account, and
      ask us to access or delete your data. Depending on where you live, you may
      have additional rights under laws such as the GDPR or CCPA; contact us to
      exercise them and we will respond as required by applicable law.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>Where data is processed</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      VisaNav is operated from the United States, and the providers above may
      process data in the United States. If you use the Service from another
      country, you understand your information will be processed here.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      We may update this policy as the Service evolves. When we make material
      changes, we will update the date at the top of this page.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>Contact</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      Questions about your privacy? Email
      <a class={a} href="mailto:privacy@visanav.org">privacy@visanav.org</a>.
      See also our
      <a class={a} href="/terms">Terms of Use</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
